From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: skip CUDA language on riscv64

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no riscv64 CI to validate against yet]

The top-level project() call enables CMake's CUDA language on every
platform except APPLE, independent of the runtime SAPIEN_CUDA option
(setup.py sets -DSAPIEN_CUDA=OFF when CUDA_PATH is unset, but that
cache variable isn't read until after project() already ran).
Enabling the CUDA language makes CMake require a CUDA compiler at
configure time even when SAPIEN_CUDA will end up OFF, which fails
outright on riscv64 runners with no CUDA toolkit. aarch64 wheels are
built with CUDA on via the sbsa toolkit (Jetson/Grace), so this isn't
an aarch64-style fix -- it needs the same treatment as macOS, which
never had a CUDA story either.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18 FATAL_ERROR)
-if (APPLE)
+if (APPLE OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "riscv64")
     project(sapien LANGUAGES C CXX)
 else()
     project(sapien LANGUAGES C CXX CUDA)
--
2.50.1
